ὀξῠ-βόαςandὀξῠ-βόης,ου,ὁ,
shrill-screaming,of birds, A. Ag. 57 ; of men, Luc. JTr. 31 ;
sharp-buzzing,of mosquitoes, AP 5.150 ( Mel. ).

ὀξῠ́-κομος,ον,
with pointed hair,of the porcupine, Opp. C. 2.599 ; of a stag, ib. 194 ; of a pine, App.Anth. 5.46 ;
with pointed spines,of a fish, Marc.Sid. 21 .

